AN ORDINANCE TO PROVIDE FOR THE SALARY OF THE MAYOR AND MEMBERS OF THE TOWN COUNCIL OF THE TOWN OF CLERMONT, GEORGIA; TO PROVIDE FOR AN EFFECTIVE DATE AND TO REPEAL CONFLICTING ORDINANCES; AND FOR OTHER LAWFUL PURPOSES:

WHEREAS, the Mayor and Town Council have previously been compensated on a basis of $35.00 and $25.00 each month, respectively, for each regularly scheduled monthly meeting attended;

WHEREAS, both the Mayor and Council received $25.00 each for additional monthly meetings;

WHEREAS, the number of meetings may vary from month to month;

WHEREAS, the Town Council deems it necessary to establish a static salary for the elected officials, so that budget figures can be accurately estimated;

THEREFORE, BE IT ORDAINED, by the Town Council of Clermont, Georgia, and it is hereby ordained by the authority of Section 2- 103 of the Town Charter, as amended, Art. 1X, Sec. II, Para. II of the Georgia Constitution of 1983, as amended, and 0.C.G.A. § 36-35-

4, as amended;
